"""_probe_dict_in_i64.spy — segfault repro, now closed at compile time.

History: `<i64> in Dict[i64, i64]` used to crash the VM (segfault on Linux)
because the runtime dict keys on strings only while the typechecker placed no
restriction on the key type.

As of Wave-1 Lane D, `Dict[i64, _]` (any non-`str` key) is a hard compile
error (E2072) instead of a silent compile-then-segfault. The original repro
body therefore no longer compiles; see `compiler/tests/conformance_negative.rs`
(`dict_i64_key_rejected`) for the negative test that pins the new behaviour.

This file is kept as a *compilable* str-key demonstration of `k in d`.
"""


fn main() -> i32:
    di: Dict[str, i64] = {}
    di["one"] = 10i64
    di["two"] = 20i64
    # `in` tests key membership (Python semantics).
    if "one" in di:
        println("present")
    else:
        println("absent")
    return 0
